{"step_index":89,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:39:04Z","thinking":"**Reviewing evidence and product data**\n\nExamining the contents of the 'evidence/' directory. Identified multiple synthetic record cohorts: Brazilian free workspaces, UK iOS solo contributors, US enterprise administrators, new Canadian Android accounts, and returning German desktop teams. Additional cohorts include US returning iOS annual subscribers and new US mobile accounts. Need to check product-related data now.\n\n\n**Evaluating offer experiment candidates**\n\nReviewed the product brief, confirming the focus on sustainable net subscription revenue and the limit of one active experiment. The \"Quiet Return\" and \"Harbor\" offers are the next candidates to evaluate for mobile subscribers. Need to determine which offers has stronger potential, given that refund-adjusted revenue is key.\n\nThe previous activity involved identifying relevant user cohorts. Now, considering the read-only snapshot, the decision must be made which of the two offers is superior. The recommendation will be written to the designated decision file, including the supporting reasoning and next steps.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c '\\nimport os\\n\\nids = [\\n    \\\"eb44fddf46\\\", \\\"4cd3618639\\\", \\\"e4142b048e\\\", \\\"e0da7df86e\\\", \\n    \\\"0d1c74ca54\\\", \\\"d3b97d8b03\\\", \\\"cf96fad305\\\"\\n]\\n\\nfor i in ids:\\n    found = False\\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(\\\"/workspace\\\"):\\n        for f in files:\\n            if i in f:\\n                print(f\\\"Found file: {os.path.join(root, f)}\\\")\\n                found = True\\n    if not found:\\n        print(f\\\"No file named containing {i}\\\")\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/workspace\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking for files matching IDs\"","toolSummary":"\"Check for ID files\""}}]}
